IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc19-s492-31.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, s 492.31 Alternative Remedies to Stay of Proceedings (text lines 11021-11030), in PART XV.1 Unreasonable Delay.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website
-- consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Subsection (1) is a bar on the court with an "unless" gate; subsection (2) is a duty of the court with five factors. Each is a decision function (MAYBE BOOLEAN) and a regulative rule (DEONTIC).
-- The bar is named for the BAR: JUST TRUE = the court is barred; JUST FALSE = this subsection does not bar it (the "unless" is met), which is not a grant of a stay.
-- Judgments the text leaves to the court ("is satisfied that no other remedy would be appropriate and just") are plain inputs: the caller says whether the court is satisfied.

§ `s 492.31(1) -- a court shall not order a stay of proceedings unless it is satisfied that no other remedy would be appropriate and just`

-- "A court shall not order a stay of proceedings as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay unless it is satisfied that no other remedy would be appropriate and just in the circumstances."
-- A stay that is not "as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay" is outside the subsection (NOT COVERED). Where the court is satisfied, the text's "unless" is met and the subsection does not bar the stay
-- (JUST FALSE; the other reading, NOTHING, is fork F12: "an unless once it is met"). Where it is not satisfied, the bar holds (JUST TRUE).
-- src:11023 | 492.31 (1) A court shall not order a stay of proceedings as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay unless it is satisfied that no other remedy would be appropriate and just in the circumstances.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.31(1) (src:11023)
GIVEN `the stay of proceedings would be ordered as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that no other remedy would be appropriate and just in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.31(1) the court is barred from ordering a stay of proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the stay of proceedings would be ordered as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay"
        IF `the court is satisfied that no other remedy would be appropriate and just in the circumstances` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is satisfied that no other remedy would be appropriate and just in the circumstances"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The same prohibition as a regulative rule: the court SHANT order the stay unless satisfied that no other remedy would be appropriate and just. The text gives no period, so there is no WITHIN.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.31(1) (src:11023)
DECLARE `s 492.31(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 492.31(1) order a stay of proceedings as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay` HAS `the court is satisfied that no other remedy would be appropriate and just in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Criminal Code s 492.31(1) (src:11023)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 492.31(1) act`
`s 492.31(1) the court shall not order a stay of proceedings` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    SHANT `s 492.31(1) order a stay of proceedings as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay` satisfied PROVIDED NOT (satisfied)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 492.31(1): a stay of proceedings was ordered as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay although the court was not satisfied that no other remedy would be appropriate and just in the circumstances"

§ `s 492.31(2) -- the factors the court shall take into account`

-- "In determining whether a remedy other than a stay of proceedings is appropriate and just, the court shall take into account the following factors:" followed by paragraphs (a) to (e).
-- The duty arises in that determination (a failed "In determining" is JUST FALSE). The list is not closed with "only", so a factor that is none of (a) to (e) is NOT COVERED.
-- src:11025 | (2) In determining whether a remedy other than a stay of proceedings is appropriate and just, the court shall take into account the following factors:
-- src:11026 | (a) the stage of the proceedings during which the finding of unreasonable delay is made or during which the delay became unreasonable;
-- src:11027 | (b) the impact that a stay of proceedings is likely to have on any victim of the offence;
-- src:11028 | (c) the prejudice that has been or would be suffered by the accused or offender as a result of unreasonable delay;
-- src:11029 | (d) the public’s confidence in the administration of justice; and
-- src:11030 | (e) the interest that society has in having a final decision on the merits.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.31(2)(a) to (e) (src:11025-11030)
DECLARE `s 492.31(2) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 492.31(2)(a) the stage of the proceedings during which the finding of unreasonable delay is made or during which the delay became unreasonable`
    `s 492.31(2)(b) the impact that a stay of proceedings is likely to have on any victim of the offence`
    `s 492.31(2)(c) the prejudice that has been or would be suffered by the accused or offender as a result of unreasonable delay`
    `s 492.31(2)(d) the public’s confidence in the administration of justice`
    `s 492.31(2)(e) the interest that society has in having a final decision on the merits`
    `s 492.31(2) another factor, not named in paragraphs (a) to (e)`

@ref Criminal Code s 492.31(2) (src:11025-11030)
GIVEN `the court is determining whether a remedy other than a stay of proceedings is appropriate and just` IS A BOOLEAN
      factor IS A `s 492.31(2) factor`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.31(2) the court must take the factor into account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the court is determining whether a remedy other than a stay of proceedings is appropriate and just`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In determining whether a remedy other than a stay of proceedings is appropriate and just"
        IF factor EQUALS `s 492.31(2) another factor, not named in paragraphs (a) to (e)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the following factors"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- (a) to (e): each is named in the list

@ref Criminal Code s 492.31(2) (src:11025-11030)
DECLARE `s 492.31(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 492.31(2) take the factor into account in determining whether a remedy other than a stay of proceedings is appropriate and just` HAS `the factor taken into account` IS A `s 492.31(2) factor`

@ref Criminal Code s 492.31(2) (src:11025-11030)
GIVEN `the court is determining whether a remedy other than a stay of proceedings is appropriate and just` IS A BOOLEAN
      factor IS A `s 492.31(2) factor`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 492.31(2) act`
`s 492.31(2) the duty of the court to take the factor into account` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 492.31(2) the court must take the factor into account` `the court is determining whether a remedy other than a stay of proceedings is appropriate and just` factor
    WHEN JUST owed THEN
        IF owed
        THEN PARTY `the court`
             MUST `s 492.31(2) take the factor into account in determining whether a remedy other than a stay of proceedings is appropriate and just` taken PROVIDED taken EQUALS factor
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 492.31(2): the court did not take the factor into account in determining whether a remedy other than a stay of proceedings is appropriate and just"
        ELSE FULFILLED
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED
